In the branch/supertuxkart/skidding version you will find out some
different behaviors in playing the game.

Note that this is a trial version which is only tested on the race
track.
Computer karts can not deal with this new behavior. It's not worth
to play it with computer karts.

Start the game from command line with:
supertuxkart -N --track race --numkarts 1



PLAYING THE BRANCH
==================

To accelerate use your usual accelerate button.
When you achive the speed you want just stop accelerating and your
kart will maintain the speed.
Think of a accelerotor pedal that you push more and more when you
push the accelerate button. Braking is vice versa.
The original wheelie button is used as a kick-down button. It shifts
the gear down if possible and pushes the accelerotor pedal completely.
The kick-down saves the pedal position so when you end kick-down
you will go on with the pedal (speed) you had before kick-down.

The faster you go your friction will decrease.
When you go to fast in curves you will see that your kart does not
follow the steering, that's the moment when skidding starts.
So brake befor entering the curve.
When you brake IN a curve within a certain speed you will see that
the rear of the kart will lift up and that's the moment you should
kick-down and steer against to maintain control. If not you will
find your kart outside the track.

Included in the src directory is a history.dat.gz file which shows how
it works in the game. To look at this history file, first uncompress
it, and then start STK as:
./supertuxkart --history
from the src directory.